{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pulls/12332","id":4156105558,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOCjvss73uSNW","html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12332","diff_url":"https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12332.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12332.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12332","number":12332,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(llm): normalize tool_call arguments from JSON string to object before template render","user":{"login":"peilii","id":76031090,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MDMxMDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76031090?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii","html_url":"https://github.com/peilii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nGLM-5.2's Jinja chat template calls `.items()` on `tool_calls[*].function.arguments`, expecting a dict. The OpenAI wire format carries arguments as a JSON string. In multi-turn conversations where the assistant's previous turn contained tool calls, the template renderer receives a string where it expects a dict, producing empty or garbled argument output.\n\n**Before** (arguments as JSON string passed to the template):\n```\ntemplate sees: tc.function.arguments = '{\"path\": \"/tmp/foo\"}'\n.items() on a string → empty iteration\nrendered:      <tool_call>read_file</tool_call>\n```\n\n**After** (arguments normalized to a dict before the template):\n```\ntemplate sees: tc.function.arguments = {\"path\": \"/tmp/foo\"}\n.items() works correctly\nrendered:      <tool_call>read_file<arg_key>path</arg_key><arg_value>/tmp/foo</arg_value></tool_call>\n```\n\nThis matches TRT-LLM's behavior: `chat_utils.py` always calls `json.loads(arguments)` before `apply_chat_template` when the value is a string. No template detection or thread-local plumbing is needed — `normalize_tool_call_arguments()` is called unconditionally in `messages()` for all three `OAIChatLikeRequest` implementors (`NvCreateChatCompletionRequest`, `UnifiedRequest`, `SpeculativePrefillRequest`). Non-object and malformed-JSON values are replaced with `{}` with a warning (byte length only — no raw content in logs).\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo build -p dynamo-llm`: clean, zero warnings\n- `cargo test -p dynamo-llm`: all tests pass\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps -p dynamo-llm -- -D warnings`: clean\n- `cargo fmt --check -p dynamo-llm`: clean\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved compatibility for tool calls by consistently normalizing function arguments before messages are processed.\n  * Invalid or incorrectly formatted tool-call arguments are now safely converted to an empty object instead of causing processing issues.\n  * Applied the same handling across standard, speculative prefill, and unified chat requests.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-07-29T00:23:31Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T19:32:07Z","closed_at":"2026-08-11T19:32:06Z","merged_at":"2026-08-11T19:32:06Z","merge_commit_sha":"b56aaf324348c35faf043ee1fb6cd150fd3e2e9b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":8457732700,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOCjvss8AAAAB-B7CXA","url":"https://api.github.com/